WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.155
Give a cheap model a job: read this invoice and return its fields.

2
00:00:05.155 --> 00:00:08.950
The planner here is DeepSeek V4 Flash, priced per call.

3
00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:15.014
It writes a plan, then asks six cheap workers to try it, one after another.

4
00:00:15.014 --> 00:00:17.240
The workers are GLM 5.3 Flash.

5
00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:20.875
Each one gets the task and returns a full answer.

6
00:00:21.375 --> 00:00:23.892
Every call is recorded with its price.

7
00:00:23.892 --> 00:00:28.462
The plan took about twenty seconds, and each worker call about three.

8
00:00:28.462 --> 00:00:31.375
This whole run cost about a tenth of a cent.

9
00:00:31.875 --> 00:00:34.043
The planner picks the best answer.

10
00:00:34.043 --> 00:00:35.382
Here all six matched.

11
00:00:35.382 --> 00:00:39.525
Then a plain check, with no model judging, marks it pass or fail.

12
00:00:40.025 --> 00:00:43.432
Same task, two teams, the same cheap workers.

13
00:00:43.432 --> 00:00:47.975
One planner is DeepSeek V4 Flash, the other DeepSeek V4 Pro.

14
00:00:47.975 --> 00:00:48.732
Both pass.

15
00:00:48.732 --> 00:00:55.850
One run cost zero point zero zero one nine dollars, the other zero point zero zero eight five.

16
00:00:56.350 --> 00:01:01.829
Run the cheapest team sixteen times: fourteen passes, about a tenth of a cent each.

17
00:01:01.829 --> 00:01:07.375
Four of those answered without delegating; of the twelve that delegated, ten passed.

18
00:01:07.875 --> 00:01:11.969
Orchestral records every run, so the numbers can be checked.

19
00:01:11.969 --> 00:01:16.200
Compare model teams on pass rate and cost per pass, then pick.
